# Shell scripts and the POSIX service templates are executed or parsed on
# Linux, macOS and Termux, where a CR breaks them: a shebang ending in \r finds
# no interpreter, and an ExecStart with \r is "command not found". They are LF
# in the repository and stay LF in every working tree, whatever the machine's
# core.autocrlf says (a Windows checkout used to hand them over with CRLF).
# The Windows templates (Task Scheduler XML, VBS launcher) are left to the
# default: schtasks reads the UTF-16 file install writes, wscript takes both.
*.sh text eol=lf
pi-extension/service-templates/systemd.service.template text eol=lf
pi-extension/service-templates/launchd.plist.template text eol=lf
pi-extension/service-templates/termux-boot.template text eol=lf
